yle=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:23:05-07:00","id":906867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/906679-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-martial-arts-wushu-wisdom?p=906865#post906865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i know that, but Martial Artists are still possible as mortals. The styles grant form weapons, philosophies and combat styles for heroic mortals</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they conceivably buy into the styles required for these fusion styles, can't they do the same thing here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T04:20:32-07:00","id":907057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/906679-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-martial-arts-wushu-wisdom?p=906865#post906865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i know that, but Martial Artists are still possible as mortals. The styles grant form weapons, philosophies and combat styles for heroic mortals</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Wushu styles still enable those things.<br /> <br /> The White Veil Society would be a secret society that practices both Throne Shadow and Dreaming Pearl Courtesan- and in their teaching, synthesize the two into a whole greater than the sum of the parts.<br /> <br /> The out of game thinking (for me, anyways) behind the Wushu styles is multi-fold;<br /> A) Sidereals are going to be incentivized to buy lots of martial arts; the Wushu arts give them another benefit for doing so.<br /> B) They provide an obvious outlet for homebrew and creativity; a means of expanding martial arts without breaking the design principle of martial arts styles being closed.<br /> C) They make it easier, not harder, to have one off secret techniques hidden in mortal societies or held by only one master-on-the-mountain; you don't have to explain or create an entire style to capture a single effect. Rather, you have to find the place where the effect arises out of two style touching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T05:58:38-07:00","id":907579,"title":"","content":"Not really what I would be looking for personally in Sidereal takes on martial arts, but that's just personal feel.<br /> <br /> I would add that, yes, fine mortals can be learning Cobra Style without specific mechanical expression, the same as they can with the &quot;non-Wushu&quot; styles, but then there's a weird question of when they Exalt as a Solar or a Dragonblooded and find that they are only expressing Snake and Black Claw Techniques. So do we then continue on with the idea that the Solar or Dragonblood is practicing the Cobra Style (Wushu), which has a strange disconnect that they won't be using any Charms for it, or do we then acknowledge that they actually aren't?<br /> <br /> Or am I misunderstanding these techniques, and they can learnt by Solars and Dragonblooded (and in which case, what is &quot;the Sidereals are uniquely aware of subtle interplays that exist between styles&quot; about)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T07:37:06-07:00","id":907624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/906679-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-martial-arts-wushu-wisdom?p=907579#post907579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really what I would be looking for personally in Sidereal takes on martial arts, but that's just personal feel.<br /> <br /> I would add that, yes, fine mortals can be learning Cobra Style without specific mechanical expression, the same as they can with the &quot;non-Wushu&quot; styles, but then there's a weird question of when they Exalt as a Solar or a Dragonblooded and find that they are only expressing Snake and Black Claw Techniques. So do we then continue on with the idea that the Solar or Dragonblood is practicing the Cobra Style (Wushu), which has a strange disconnect that they won't be using any Charms for it, or do we then acknowledge that they actually aren't?<br /> <br /> Or am I misunderstanding these techniques, and they can learnt by Solars and Dragonblooded (and in which case, what is &quot;the Sidereals are uniquely aware of subtle interplays that exist between styles&quot; about)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The motions and philosophies behind the wushu styles can be learned by anyone who can learn the motions and philosophies of the parent styles- which is most anyone who can buy the Martial Arts merit. They don't have a mechanical representation beyond skill with the parent abilities, because it felt like a pointless xp sink- but you can still totally have a White Veil Society that keeps alive the traditions, ideas and practices of White Veil Style.<br /> <br /> The charms of wushu styles can be learned by anyone who can learn the parent styles- so, pretty much, the Exalted. The Wushu styles are *emphatically* not Sidereal Martial Arts- anyone can learn them. The 'uniquely aware of the subtle interplay' thing... well, I'll confess, my initial conceptualization of the Wushu arts was that only the Sidereals could discover them, but that any of the Exalted could be taught them. I think, on reflection (between you and Growls both emphasizing a desire for a mortal tradition of Cobra), that's a poor choice. The Sidereals are more casually aware of the Wushu arts, because they're incentivized to buy into multiple martial arts styles and discover the synergies within them- but there is relatively little value in forcing that restriction. I'll be amending that text; something more likely 'while Sidereals are unusually aware of the subtle interplay between different martial arts, any of the Exalted who practice the parent styles may independently discover the Wushu arts for themselves'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}